Disclosed herein is a method for processing cocoa beans or nibs, comprising the following steps:

(a) adding water to cocoa beans or nibs to form a suspension;

(b) subjecting said suspension to wet grinding;

(c) treating said suspension with heat at a temperature of 70°C or below;

(d) separating the suspension into three distinct phases: a water phase (heavy phase); a fat phase (light phase) comprising cocoa butter; and a solid phase comprising cocoa powder and fluid components;

(e) continuously separating the fluid components from the solid phase obtained in step (d) to yield cocoa aroma and cocoa powder, achieved by directing a flow of said solid phase into a mixing device;

wherein the mixing device comprises:

- a cylindrical, tubular body oriented along a horizontal axis, featuring an inlet opening for the solid phase, an outlet opening for the dried solid phase, and an optional outlet opening for a vapor phase comprising cocoa aroma;

- end plates that seal the tubular body at its opposing ends;

- a coaxial jacket configured to heat or cool the internal wall of the tubular body to a temperature ranging from 55°C to 150°C; and

- a bladed rotor, rotatably supported within the tubular body, the blades of which are arranged in a helical configuration and oriented so as to centrifuge the solid phase while simultaneously conveying it toward the outlet opening.
